# Local secrets. Real IPTV provider credentials used for playback testing live
# here and must never reach the history: they unlock a third-party account.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Runtime env. Carries APP_KEY and is bundled as a Flutter asset, so it is
# readable in a shipped web build. `.env.example` is the tracked template and a
# release build has to provision the real file.
.env

# Personal per-machine instructions, by convention not committed.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Agent runtime state. `.ac/research/` and `.ac/plans/` are deliberate project
# artefacts and stay tracked; `.ac/state/` is per-run bookkeeping.
.ac/state/

# pubspec.lock IS committed: this is an application and a deploy without a lock
# is not reproducible. The catch is that a lock generated while
# pubspec_overrides.yaml is active encodes sibling paths that exist on no CI
# runner, including a relative one that resolves to nothing from a worktree. So
# the committed lock is the hosted-only one:
#
#   mv pubspec_overrides.yaml /tmp/ && flutter pub get && git add pubspec.lock
#   mv /tmp/pubspec_overrides.yaml . && flutter pub get
#
# Day-to-day local `pub get` runs dirty the lock with paths. Leave those
# unstaged rather than committing them.

# Local dependency overrides pointing at the sibling fluttersdk checkouts.
# Committing this would force every contributor onto absolute paths from one
# machine. Listed in .worktreeinclude so a worktree still gets a copy.
pubspec_overrides.yaml
.artisan/

# Snapshots, console logs and screenshots dropped by `playwright-cli` next to
# wherever it was run. Session artefacts, and it writes them without asking.
.playwright-cli/
